userStories.description:
**Goal** — Add the public bounded CI failure reader, URL/excerpt helpers and GitHub implementation in packages/nax/src/forge/ci-failures.ts.

**Motivation** — Fixing them is manual today.

**Approach** — Logs come from the forge CLI through a new `readFailedChecks` in `src/forge/ci-failures.ts`. The argv shapes were probed live on GitHub (koda) and GitLab (store-erp) on 2026-10-21.

### CI failure reader (`src/forge/ci-failures.ts`, exported from `@/forge`)

```ts
export interface FailedCheck {
  readonly name: string;
  readonly url?: string;
  readonly excerpt: string;
}
export const MAX_FAILED_CHECKS = 5;
export const CI_EXCERPT_LINES = 200;
export const CI_EXCERPT_CHARS = 8_000;
export function prNumberFromUrl(url: string): number | null;
export function ciExcerpt(log: string): string;
export async function readFailedChecks(
  ref: PrRef,
  headSha: string,
  deps: ForgeDeps,
  cwd: string,
): Promise<readonly FailedCheck[]>;
```

- **`prNumberFromUrl`:** the number after `/pull/` (GitHub) or `/merge_requests/` (GitLab), optionally followed by `/`, `?` or `#`. It returns `null` for anything else.
- **`ciExcerpt`:** removes ANSI CSI escape sequences (ESC `[` ... final byte), keeps the last `CI_EXCERPT_LINES` lines, then the last `CI_EXCERPT_CHARS` characters, then applies `redactSecrets`.
- **GitHub:**
  1. Call `["gh", "api", "--hostname", ref.host, "repos/<repo>/commits/<headSha>/check-runs?per_page=100&filter=latest"]`. The reply is `{ check_runs: [{ id, name, conclusion, html_url, app: { slug }, output: { title, summary, text } }] }`. Only this first page is read.
  2. A check run failed when its `conclusion` is non-null and not `success`, `skipped` or `neutral`. This covers `failure`, `timed_out`, `cancelled`, `startup_failure`, `action_required` and `stale`, so every check the CI wait counts as failed is listed. The first `MAX_FAILED_CHECKS` failed runs are kept, in reply order.
  3. For `app.slug` `github-actions`, the log comes from `["gh", "run", "view", "--job", "<id>", "--log-failed", "-R", "<host>/<repo>"]`. For a GitHub Actions check run, its id is the job id (verified live).
  4. For any other app, the excerpt input is the non-empty values among `output.title`, `output.summary` and `output.text`, joined with `\n`, or `(no output)` when all three are empty.
  5. `url` is `html_url`.

**Scope** — In: create the source and test/unit/forge/ci-failures.test.ts, and export the interface, constants and functions from the existing forge barrel. Reuse `PrRef`, `ForgeDeps` and the existing `redactSecrets` logger export; every command uses injected deps and cwd. Out: GitLab and shared error completion belong to US-002; workflow decision/graph/production wiring belong to US-006–US-008. Legacy GitHub commit statuses (the statuses API) are not read, only check runs, and only the first 100 check runs of a commit. No retrying jobs or model calls.

**Interface** — The TypeScript block above is the public contract; US-006 consumes FailedCheck only as a type and US-008 becomes the production readFailedChecks caller. Tests import these symbols through @/forge so missing exports fail locally. Use mocked ForgeDeps, exact argv assertions and bounded-output assertions; never call a live forge.
